{"tool_name":"deltag_prediction","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"deltag_prediction","home":"http://dgpred.cbr.su.se/","summary":"Prediction of apparent free energy difference for a potential transmembrane helix.","addition_date":"2015-12-06T15:18:12Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:33:08.023284Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"version":["1"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:deltag_prediction","credit":[{"email":"gunnar@dbb.su.se","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"bils.se","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://dgpred.cbr.su.se/index.php?p=instructions"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"}}],"operation":[{"term":"Prediction and recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2423"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1277"}}]}],"name":"DeltaG prediction","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"mikael.borg@bils.se","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/nature06387","metadata":{"abstract":"Transmembrane \u03b1-helices in integral membrane proteins are recognized co-translationally and inserted into the membrane of the endoplasmic reticulum by the Sec61 translocon. A full quantitative description of this phenomenon, linking amino acid sequence to membrane insertion efficiency, is still lacking. Here, using in vitro translation of a model protein in the presence of dog pancreas rough microsomes to analyse a large number of systematically designed hydrophobic segments, we present a quantitative analysis of the position-dependent contribution of all 20 amino acids to membrane insertion efficiency, as well as of the effects of transmembrane segment length and flanking amino acids. The emerging picture of translocon-mediated transmembrane helix assembly is simple, with the critical sequence characteristics mirroring the physical properties of the lipid bilayer. \u00a92007 Nature Publishing Group.","authors":[{"name":"Bernsel A."},{"name":"Hessa T."},{"name":"Kim H."},{"name":"Lerch-Bader M."},{"name":"Meindl-Beinker N.M."},{"name":"Nilsson I."},{"name":"Sato Y."},{"name":"Von Heijne G."},{"name":"White S.H."}],"citationCount":567,"date":"2007-12-13T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature","title":"Molecular code for transmembrane-helix recognition by the Sec61 translocon"},"pmid":"18075582","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein folds and structural domains","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0736"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DeltaG prediction","home":"https://bio.tools/deltag_prediction","version":"1","summary":"Prediction of apparent free energy difference for a potential transmembrane helix.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:deltag_prediction:1/web/dgpred.cbr.su.se","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":395,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":8,"year":"2024"},{"count":11,"year":"2008"},{"count":11,"year":"2026"},{"count":12,"year":"2022"},{"count":16,"year":"2023"},{"count":17,"year":"2010"},{"count":17,"year":"2016"},{"count":18,"year":"2020"},{"count":20,"year":"2018"},{"count":22,"year":"2015"},{"count":23,"year":"2009"},{"count":23,"year":"2025"},{"count":24,"year":"2011"},{"count":25,"year":"2019"},{"count":26,"year":"2012"},{"count":26,"year":"2017"},{"count":28,"year":"2013"},{"count":29,"year":"2021"},{"count":38,"year":"2014"}],"doi":"10.1038/nature06387","pmid":"18075582","ref_count":0,"refs":[],"title":"Molecular code for transmembrane-helix recognition by the Sec61 translocon.","year":2007}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"biosch